   "title": "Korea, African Union discuss cooperation fund, broader ties",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/foreignaffairs/20261104/korea-african-union-discuss-cooperation-fund-broader-ties",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Wed, 04 Nov 2026 07:12:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793776323.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "Korea and the African Union (AU) have discussed ways to manage their joint cooperation fund and expand economic, healthcare and other forms of cooperation, Seoul's foreign ministry said Wednesday. During the meeting, the two sides discussed ways to manage the Korea-AU Cooperation Fund and expand substantive cooperation in trade, investment, healthcare, youth and women's empowerment, climate change and peace and security, among other fields.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国与非洲联盟（AU）于星期三讨论了管理双方合作基金以及扩大经济、医疗保健及其他领域合作的方法。这是韩国外交部星期三发布的声明。会谈期间，双方讨论了管理韩国—非洲联盟合作基金的办法，并商定扩大贸易、投资、医疗保健、青年和女性赋权、气候变化以及和平与安全等领域的实质性合作。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea and the African Union (AU) have discussed ways to manage their joint cooperation fund and expand economic, healthcare and other forms of cooperation, Seoul's foreign ministry said Wednesday. The discussions took place during the seventh round of policy consultations in Addis Ababa on Tuesday (local time), with Chung Kwang-yong, director-general for African and Middle Eastern affairs at the ministry, and Willy Nyamitwe, chairperson of the AU's Permanent Representatives Committee, leading their delegations, according to the ministry. Established in 2002, the 54-member AU aims to promote African integration, peace and security. During the meeting, the two sides discussed ways to manage the Korea-AU Cooperation Fund and expand substantive cooperation in trade, investment, healthcare, youth and women's empowerment, climate change and peace and security, among other fields. Korea shared updates on its cooperation projects with Africa and proposed expanding ties through high-level exchanges. The AU welcomed Seoul's continued commitment and pledged to support mutually beneficial cooperation, the ministry said",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
