   "summary": "British and Korean policymakers, lawmakers and artificial intelligence (AI) experts will gather in Seoul on Thursday to examine how their countries can strengthen AI competitiveness and cooperate on national strategies as governments confront the policy challenges posed by rapidly advancing technology. GR Korea and the British Chamber of Commerce in Korea will co-host a breakfast briefing titled \"Politics of AI Breakfast: AI and National Strategy with BCCK\" on Thursday at Conrad Seoul.",
   "summary_zh": "英国和韩国的政策制定者、议员及人工智能（AI）专家将于周四在首尔举行活动，探讨两国如何在政府应对快速发展的技术所带来的政策挑战之际，加强人工智能竞争力并就国家战略开展合作。GR Korea与韩国英国商会将于周四在首尔康莱德酒店联合举办题为“人工智能早餐会：人工智能与国家战略及BCCK”的早餐简报会。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "British and Korean policymakers, lawmakers and artificial intelligence (AI) experts will gather in Seoul on Thursday to examine how their countries can strengthen AI competitiveness and cooperate on national strategies as governments confront the policy challenges posed by rapidly advancing technology. GR Korea and the British Chamber of Commerce in Korea will co-host a breakfast briefing titled \"Politics of AI Breakfast: AI and National Strategy with BCCK\" on Thursday at Conrad Seoul. Participants will include British Ambassador to Korea Colin Crooks, National Assembly member Rep. Lee Jeong-heon of the Democratic Party of Korea, and a British parliamentary delegation led by Alicia Kearns. The forum will also bring together Moon Ju-yun, executive director of GR Korea; Hong Sung-eun, a professor at Sungkyunkwan University's School of Global AI Convergence; and Lee Won-tae, chairman of the Special Committee on Security at the National AI Strategy Committee. Rep. Lee will deliver a keynote address outlining Korea's national AI strategy, major policy priorities and the respective roles of the government and National Assembly. Discussions will focus on the policy challenges surrounding AI adoption and its safe use across industries, as well as ways to strengthen the competitiveness of both countries' AI sectors. Participants will also explore opportunities for closer policy cooperation between Korea and the United Kingdom, including approaches to national AI governance and industry development. GR Korea is the Korean office of The GR Company, a government relations and public affairs consultancy operating across the Asia-Pacific region. The firm advises domestic and international companies on policy and regulatory developments, government and parliamentary relations, and engagement with key stakeholders. This article was published with the assistance of generative AI and edited by The Korea Times",
