   "title": "Kotak Mahindra Bank gets CCI nod to acquire Deutsche Bank India's retail, private banking businesses",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/business/Industry/kotak-mahindra-bank-gets-cci-nod-to-acquire-deutsche-bank-indias-retail-private-banking-businesses/article71664408.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:23:01 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793775181.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Kotak Mahindra Bank has secured the Competition Commission of India’s (CCI) approval to take over Deutsche Bank's retail banking, private banking and wealth management business in the country, marking a proposed transfer of the German lender's customer-facing businesses to the domestic bank.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后解锁 Kotak Mahindra Bank已获得印度竞争委员会（CCI）的批准，将接管德意志银行在印度的零售银行、私人银行和财富管理业务。这意味着这家德国贷款机构面向客户的业务拟转让给本土银行。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Kotak Mahindra Bank has secured the Competition Commission of India’s (CCI) approval to take over Deutsche Bank's retail banking, private banking and wealth management business in the country, marking a proposed transfer of the German lender's customer-facing businesses to the domestic bank. The competition watchdog, on Tuesday, said it had approved the acquisition of the businesses operated by Deutsche Bank through its Indian branches. \"The proposed combination envisages acquisition of retail banking, private banking and wealth management business of Deutsche Bank Aktiengesellschaft (seller) undertaken through its branches in India (target business),\" CCI said. The transaction will be undertaken as a going concern on a slump sale basis by Kotak Mahindra Bank Ltd (acquirer) from the seller, it added. The deal also involves referral arrangements between affiliates of the two groups, under which customers of Deutsche Investments India Pvt Ltd's investment advisory and portfolio management services businesses will be referred to relevant wholly owned subsidiaries of Kotak Mahindra Bank. Deutsche Investments India is an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of Deutsche Bank. In June, Kotak Mahindra Bank and Deutsche Bank AG, acting through its India branch, said they have entered into a definitive agreement for Kotak to acquire Deutsche Bank's retail banking, affluent private banking and wealth management business in the country. The business comprises approximately ₹29,000 crore (about €2.7 billion) in loans, ₹16,000 crore (around ₹1.5 billion) in deposits and ₹10,500 crore (approximately €1 billion) of assets under management, they said. Established in 1985, Kotak Mahindra Group is one of India's leading diversified and integrated financial services conglomerates. As on March, 31 2026, the Group has total assets of ₹10,03,353 crore. Deutsche Bank is Germany's leading bank, with a strong presence in Europe and a significant footprint across the Americas and Asia Pacific. The deals beyond a certain threshold require approval from the regulator, which keeps a tab on unfair business practices as well as promotes fair competition in the marketplace. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
