   "title": "Shift to Navi Mumbai or stop flying to Mumbai: Adani Airports CEO tells foreign airlines",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/business/Industry/shift-to-navi-mumbai-or-stop-flying-to-mumbai-adani-airports-ceo-tells-foreign-airlines/article71660830.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Wed, 04 Nov 2026 10:54:04 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793769844.0,
   "ageDays": 0.09,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Adani Airport Holdings CEO Arun Bansal on Tuesday (November 3, 2026) said international airlines unwilling to shift their operations to the upcoming Navi Mumbai International Airport (NMIA) could stop flying to Mumbai. The disagreement comes as Adani-owned Mumbai International Airport Ltd. (MIAL) prepares to undertake redevelopment work at Terminal 1, necessitating the relocation of a portion of flight operations currently handled at Terminal 2 to Navi Mumbai.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅以解锁这些内容。Adani机场控股公司首席执行官Arun Bansal于周二（2026年11月3日）表示，不愿将业务转至即将启用的新孟买国际机场（NMIA）的国际航空公司，可能将停止飞往孟买。此次分歧发生时，Adani旗下孟买国际机场有限公司（MIAL）正准备对1号航站楼进行改造开发，因此需要将目前由2号航站楼处理的部分航班业务转移至新孟买。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Adani Airport Holdings CEO Arun Bansal on Tuesday (November 3, 2026) said international airlines unwilling to shift their operations to the upcoming Navi Mumbai International Airport (NMIA) could stop flying to Mumbai. The disagreement comes as Adani-owned Mumbai International Airport Ltd. (MIAL) prepares to undertake redevelopment work at Terminal 1, necessitating the relocation of a portion of flight operations currently handled at Terminal 2 to Navi Mumbai. The proposed shift has faced resistance from international airlines, which have raised concerns over the lack of adequate consultation, the impact on passengers and the operational implications of splitting their Mumbai operations between two airports. Defending the airport operator’s position, Mr. Bansal said airlines had been given notice to vacate the existing facilities from April, adding that where they chose to operate subsequently was their decision. “Like a landlord tells its airlines to vacate his property… we have told airlines you have to vacate from April. After that where you go is your choice,” he told reporters on the sidelines of the India Aviation Summit 2026. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
